\\"1.0\\\" is the initial agreement. An omitted release selects the current agreement; an explicit supported release selects that version. Versions introduced in an issue remain supported afterward; public suites name a specific release and send explicit release values, so their expectations survive changes to the current agreement.\n\nImplementation: main.py encodes the agreement generally in assign_credits_1_0 (one cap pass over a whole statement line list). quote_1_0 applies it to a single supplied line treated as the entire statement; total_1_0 applies it to the complete statement \\\"lines\\\" list and returns exactly release, credit_cents (sum of assigned credits), and amount_due_cents (total charges minus total credit), so a total is never a sum of independent single-line quotes. statement_1_0 returns exactly release, lines, credit_cents, and amount_due_cents, each response line carrying exactly line_id, credit_cents, and amount_due_cents in the request line input order, with overall amounts equal to the total response for the same input; empty input returns lines [] with zero totals. Verified by the explicit release-1.0 cases of tests/test_quote.py, tests/test_total.py, and tests/test_statement.py, and by public_tests/release_1_quote.json, public_tests/release_1_total.json, and public_tests/release_1_statement.json (full suite, 33 tests, and all five public suites re-run OK in trial-878 on 2026-09-07).\"",
